purpose_raw:
The funds will be used to provide after and summer school programs.
Programs include Education, Technology, and Career programs;
Character/Leadership Development programs.

Build, strengthen and sustain the governing body of the Bed Stuy Works
Alliance (a coalition of Block and Tenant Associations in Bedford
Stuyvesant) and document for replication in other neighborhoods;

Funding to support music programming in CD 43 at PS 112 Lefferts Park;
PS 102 The Bay View School and  Seniors in Touch (Services for Older
Adults).

To support in-school and after-school programs in Council District 1;
tournaments at public schools; college-bound program; and teacher
training institute.

Funds will support Civil Legal Services in CD28. Services include housing;
education; foreclosure prevention; homeless rights; govt benefits;
employment; immigration; family/DV; law reform; consumer, elder and
disability law; & community development.

Funding to implement and maintain a district-wide cleanup initiative;
Project Sweep will clean commercial strips and/or other areas in the
community.

Funds to help Chess in the Schools Programming and Summer Camps;
Tournament Program; College Bound and Project Chess Teacher
Training Institute.
